<node id="Connection Pool Exhaustion">
  <data key="d0">Connection Pool Exhaustion</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Connection Pool Exhaustion is a critical system-level issue that occurs when all available connections within a predefined connection pool are simultaneously in use, preventing new connections from being established. This depletion of connection resources leads to service slowdowns, delayed responses, dropped requests, or complete system failures, particularly in environments requiring consistent accessibility to databases, network services, or other critical resources. The condition is commonly observed across various technical domains, including database systems, service-oriented architectures, vector database operations, and specialized workflows like semantic caching or text compression, where finite resource limits directly impact system performance and reliability.

As a significant operational challenge, Connection Pool Exhaustion hinders a system's ability to process new requests or sustain throughput, often resulting in reduced efficiency and service unavailability. High-demand computational contexts, such as knowledge graph systems, are especially susceptible due to their reliance on finite, reusable connection pools. The issue typically arises under high load conditions or when slow queries occupy connections for extended periods. It is widely recognized as a common practical problem that should be proactively identified through stress testing or load testing before system deployment. Addressing this issue is vital for maintaining system stability, preventing disruptions, and ensuring the seamless operation of resource-intensive applications in production environments.&lt;SEP&gt;A common problem where connection pool resources are depleted, affecting system availability.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eb163727917cbba1eea208541a643e74-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f3ef77ac0e3619e98159e9b6febf557-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b1d10e7bafa4421218a51b1e1f1b0ba2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7eabe3a1649ffa2b3ff8c02ebfd5659f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-274ad4786c3abca69fa097b85867d9a4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0e65972dce68dad4d52d063967f0a705-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-85d8ce590ad8981ca2c8286f79f59954-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0336dcbab05b9d5ad24f4333c7658a0e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-bd686fd640be98efaae0091fa301e613-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-58a2fc6ed39fd083f55d4182bf88826d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a2557a7b2e94197ff767970b67041697-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-31fefc0e570cb3860f2a6d4b38c6490d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eecca5b6365d9607ee5a9d336962c534-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-65ded5353c5ee48d0b7d48c591b8f430-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9b8619251a19057cff70779273e95aa6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1afa34a7f984eeabdbb0a7d494132ee5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ec5decca5ed3d6b8079e2e7e7bacc9f2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-069059b7ef840f0c74a814ec9237b6ec-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-07e1cd7dca89a1678042477183b7ac3f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26657d5ff9020d2abefe558796b99584-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-812b4ba287f5ee0bc9d43bbf5bbe87fb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7647966b7343c29048673252e490f736-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3ef815416f775098fe977004015c6193-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fe9fc289c3ff0af142b6d3bead98a923-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28dd2c7955ce926456240b2ff0100bde-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbd7939d674997cdb4692d34de8633c4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ea5d2f1c4608232e07d3aa3d998e5135-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7f39f8317fbdb1988ef4c628eba02591-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-072b030ba126b2f4b2374f342be9ed44-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-093f65e080a295f8076b1c5722a46aa2-chunk-000</data>
