<node id="Data Preprocessing">
  <data key="d0">Data Preprocessing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Data Preprocessing is a foundational procedure within various data-driven systems, serving as the initial stage where raw data is prepared, cleaned, and formatted before entering a primary processing workflow. In the context of an evaluation benchmark system, it ensures that raw data is structured and made ready for the main analytical pipeline. Similarly, in the Document Slicing Strategy workflow, it acts as a preparatory step that transforms input data, making it suitable for subsequent processing stages.

Within the operation of a vector database, Data Preprocessing is the first step in managing incoming information, structuring it for efficient storage and retrieval. This role is also explicitly noted as a critical precursor in Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) systems, where it readies data for the main retrieval and generation workflow. Across these systems, the process consistently involves standardizing or normalizing data to ensure compatibility and consistency, which is vital for the reliability of downstream tasks.

Its importance is highlighted in both text compression workflows and batch processing systems. In text compression, it functions as the initial stage where data is normalized before the compression algorithm is applied, ensuring optimal performance. In a batch processing environment, it is the gateway step where data is cleaned and prepared for mass processing. Overall, Data Preprocessing is a universal and essential preliminary phase across these architectures, unifying the approach to data entry to maintain data quality and system efficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eb163727917cbba1eea208541a643e74-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-85d8ce590ad8981ca2c8286f79f59954-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eecca5b6365d9607ee5a9d336962c534-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-069059b7ef840f0c74a814ec9237b6ec-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-07e1cd7dca89a1678042477183b7ac3f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-812b4ba287f5ee0bc9d43bbf5bbe87fb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3ef815416f775098fe977004015c6193-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ea5d2f1c4608232e07d3aa3d998e5135-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">211&lt;SEP&gt;197&lt;SEP&gt;185&lt;SEP&gt;126&lt;SEP&gt;119&lt;SEP&gt;95&lt;SEP&gt;85&lt;SEP&gt;64</data>
  <data key="d5">1788256819</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="降级">
  <data key="d0">降级</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">降级 (degradation) is a system strategy and fault-tolerance mechanism used in computing and software systems, particularly within evaluation benchmark (评估基准) systems, semantic caching systems, and streaming computation frameworks, to ensure service availability during abnormal conditions, dependency failures, high loads, or degraded performance. It functions as a proactive, fail-safe approach that automatically lowers service levels or simplifies functionality based on the real-time status of dependent services. When a dependency service fails, behaves abnormally, or encounters an exception, the system invokes a controlled degradation tactic that prioritizes core service continuity over full-feature delivery, thereby preventing complete service disruption while keeping critical operations intact.

This strategy is often paired with other resilience techniques, such as 重试 (retry), and serves as a fallback mechanism to guarantee availability when dependent services fail. It is a fundamental component of resilient system design, enabling systems to remain operational and responsive under stress. Recovery to full capacity is achieved automatically once the underlying issues are resolved, reinforcing its role in maintaining long-term system robustness and availability. The mechanism is also discussed within the context of熔断降级's principles and implementation, where it is highlighted as one of the internal methods for preserving service continuity during anomalies.&lt;SEP&gt;A degradation strategy that maintains system availability by gracefully reducing service quality when dependent services fail.&lt;SEP&gt;A fault-tolerance strategy that degrades system functionality to maintain availability when dependent services fail.&lt;SEP&gt;A fallback strategy used to guarantee availability when dependent services fail.&lt;SEP&gt;A degradation strategy used to guarantee availability when dependent services fail.&lt;SEP&gt;A degradation strategy used to maintain availability when dependency services encounter exceptions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1534b76d325a8f591b52d302e7181331-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-69adc1e107f7f7d035d7baf04342e1ca-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3644a684f98ea8fe223c713b77189a77-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-757b505cfd34c64c85ca5b5690ee5293-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-854d6fae5ee42911677c739ee1734486-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-084b6fbb10729ed4da8c3d3f5a3ae7c9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a597e50502f5ff68e3e25b9114205d4a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9fc3d7152ba9336a670e36d0ed79bc43-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1f491a404d6854880943e5c3cd9ca25-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb160de1de89d9058fcb0b968dbbbd68-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5fd0b37cd7dbbb00f97ba6ce92bf5add-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5f93f983524def3dca464469d2cf9f3e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a97da629b098b75c294dffdc3e463904-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c9e1074f5b3f9fc8ea15d152add07294-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ec8956637a99787bd197eacd77acce5e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-38b3eff8baf56627478ec76a704e9b52-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f899139df5e1059396431415e770c6dd-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ac627ab1ccbdb62ec96e702f07f6425b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98dce83da57b0395e163467c9dae521b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54229abfcfa5649e7003b83dd4755294-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c7e1249ffc03eb9ded908c236bd1996d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-68d30a9594728bc39aa24be94b319d21-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f033ab37c30201f73f142449d037028d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad61ab143223efbc24c7d2583be69251-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d2ddea18f00665ce8623e36bd4e3c7c5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-32bb90e8976aab5298d5da10fe66f21d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7cbbc409ec990f19c78c75bd1e06f215-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3f390d88e4c41f2747bfa2f1b5f87db-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3295c76acbf4caaed33c36b1b5fc2cb1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fc490ca45c00b1249bbe3554a4fdf6fb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-03afdbd66e7929b125f8597834fa83a4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f041e16a60928b05a7e228a89c3799-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a684eceee76fc522773286a895bc8436-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d82c8d1619ad8176d665453cfb2e55f0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2838023a778dfaecdc212708f721b788-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c0c7c76d30bd3dcaefc96f40275bdc0a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-67c6a1e7ce56d3d6fa748ab6d9af3fd7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-17e62166fc8586dfa4d1bc0e1742c08b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3416a75f4cea9109507cacd8e2f2aefc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d645920e395fedad7bbbed0eca3fe2e0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5771bce93e200c36f7cd9dfd0e5deaa-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">212&lt;SEP&gt;207&lt;SEP&gt;200&lt;SEP&gt;201&lt;SEP&gt;202&lt;SEP&gt;196&lt;SEP&gt;194&lt;SEP&gt;133&lt;SEP&gt;129&lt;SEP&gt;117&lt;SEP&gt;114&lt;SEP&gt;110&lt;SEP&gt;107&lt;SEP&gt;104&lt;SEP&gt;102&lt;SEP&gt;101&lt;SEP&gt;100&lt;SEP&gt;99&lt;SEP&gt;93&lt;SEP&gt;91&lt;SEP&gt;87&lt;SEP&gt;84&lt;SEP&gt;80&lt;SEP&gt;74&lt;SEP&gt;73&lt;SEP&gt;72&lt;SEP&gt;70&lt;SEP&gt;68&lt;SEP&gt;66&lt;SEP&gt;65&lt;SEP&gt;63&lt;SEP&gt;58&lt;SEP&gt;54&lt;SEP&gt;53&lt;SEP&gt;51&lt;SEP&gt;50&lt;SEP&gt;47&lt;SEP&gt;43&lt;SEP&gt;41&lt;SEP&gt;40&lt;SEP&gt;38</data>
