<node id="压测">
  <data key="d0">压测</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">压测 (Stress Testing or Pressure Testing) is a specialized performance testing methodology used to evaluate a system's behavior, stability, and resilience under high or extreme load conditions. Its primary purpose is to simulate heavy user or operational demands before deployment to a production environment, thereby uncovering potential vulnerabilities, performance bottlenecks, and weaknesses. By applying intense workloads, 压测 enables developers and engineers to identify critical performance limits and address issues that could arise during real-world use. This testing approach focuses on detecting and mitigating risks such as cache invalidation storms, cache stampede, connection pool exhaustion, and high network round-trip latency with remote services. It plays a crucial role in ensuring system reliability and robustness by exposing resource depletion and high-latency operations during peak load conditions.

While typically applied to entire software systems, 压测 can also target specific components, such as multichannel recall systems, embedding models, or vector database implementations, to optimize their performance prior to release. In contexts like熔断降级 (circuit breaking and degradation) systems, it is specifically used to reveal issues like缓存失效风暴, 连接池耗尽, and high远程服务网络往返延迟 before going live. Ultimately, the goal of 压测 is to deliver production-ready systems capable of sustaining both anticipated and extreme operational scenarios, ensuring scalability, stability, and optimal performance under real-world workloads. The methodology is consistently applied before system launch to reveal common issues, including performance bottlenecks, and it also supports parameter tuning and validation based on measured data, thereby supporting robust system validation across various technical domains. No conflicting descriptions were found across the provided sources, which uniformly describe 压测 as a pre-deployment load simulation technique with a focus on exposing systemic weaknesses and supporting performance optimization.&lt;SEP&gt;Load testing performed before deployment to expose potential system issues.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;The practice of stress testing to expose problems before deployment, also used to generate the test document.</data>
