<node id="归因分析">
  <data key="d0">归因分析</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">归因分析 (Attribution Analysis) is an analytical method and process used to identify the root causes of performance issues, particularly slow queries, and system anomalies. This technique is applied during the operation of systems such as "重排序" (re-ranking), semantic caching systems, and multi-channel recall processes. Its primary purpose is to trace performance bottlenecks back to their underlying causes by attributing them to specific factors, thereby enabling system performance improvements. The methodology involves a systematic examination of why a query is slow, breaking down contributing elements to pinpoint the exact source of the problem. While the core focus is on diagnosing slow queries, it is also applicable to broader system abnormalities or performance issues, serving as a technical approach for root cause analysis. By identifying whether the issue stems from a particular stage, component, or external condition, 归因分析 provides actionable insights that support optimization and stability of the overall system.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique used to analyze and identify the root causes of slow queries or performance issues.&lt;SEP&gt;The analysis process used to attribute causes for slow queries in monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1534b76d325a8f591b52d302e7181331-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-854d6fae5ee42911677c739ee1734486-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7f1de29e6da19d22b51c68001e7e0e54-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ec8956637a99787bd197eacd77acce5e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-68d30a9594728bc39aa24be94b319d21-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35f4a8d465e6e1edc05f3d8ab658c551-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-32bb90e8976aab5298d5da10fe66f21d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7cbbc409ec990f19c78c75bd1e06f215-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a1158154dfa42caddbd0694a4e9bdc8-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-17e62166fc8586dfa4d1bc0e1742c08b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d645920e395fedad7bbbed0eca3fe2e0-chunk-000</data>
