</node>
<node id="Degradation Mechanism">
  <data key="d0">Degradation Mechanism</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A strategy used to maintain system availability by reducing the quality or functionality of non-critical services in case of failures.&lt;SEP&gt;A fallback approach employed in systems to guarantee availability when dependent services fail.&lt;SEP&gt;A fail-safe method employed to sustain system availability even when partial functionalities are diminished.&lt;SEP&gt;A fallback strategy implemented in knowledge graph systems to maintain functionality during service dependency failures.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique implemented to maintain system availability when dependency services fail.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6f3ef77ac0e3619e98159e9b6febf557-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0e65972dce68dad4d52d063967f0a705-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-bd686fd640be98efaae0091fa301e613-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-58a2fc6ed39fd083f55d4182bf88826d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a2557a7b2e94197ff767970b67041697-chunk-000</data>
