<node id="依赖服务">
  <data key="d0">依赖服务</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">External systems or components that the primary system relies on for functionality.&lt;SEP&gt;依赖服务refers to external or downstream services that the system relies on; when these services are abnormal, the system uses retry and degradation mechanisms to ensure availability.&lt;SEP&gt;External services whose anomalies trigger retry and degradation mechanisms in the semantic caching system.&lt;SEP&gt;External services that the main system depends on, which may experience anomalies or failures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-091d584fced301b442654dd8c23b3fc9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-44f683a84163b3523afe57c2e008bc8c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c0c7c76d30bd3dcaefc96f40275bdc0a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d645920e395fedad7bbbed0eca3fe2e0-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">208&lt;SEP&gt;62&lt;SEP&gt;50&lt;SEP&gt;40</data>
  <data key="d5">1788257029</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="重试与降级">
  <data key="d0">重试与降级</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Retry and degradation (重试与降级) is a set of fault-handling techniques designed to ensure system availability when dependent services encounter errors, failures, or abnormalities. This strategy is fundamental to maintaining operational stability in distributed systems, such as vector databases, embedded model systems, and multi-channel recall systems, by implementing two complementary mechanisms. The retry mechanism automatically resends a failed request in hopes of achieving a successful outcome, while the degradation mechanism temporarily disables or simplifies non-essential features to keep the core system running despite the underlying issue.

These techniques are proactively applied when a dependent service returns an error, crashes, experiences network timeouts, or suffers resource exhaustion. By either repeating the operation or reducing service functionality, the system can continue to function—potentially with reduced capabilities—rather than failing completely. This fallback approach ensures that the system remains accessible and responsive to users even when its supporting components are unstable, making retry and degradation a core component of robust, high-availability system design.

As a resilience and reliability strategy, retry and degradation is employed to maintain availability when dependent services behave abnormally or fail. It is particularly critical in multi-channel recall systems, where it ensures continuous operation by retrying failed operations and degrading functionality as needed. Ultimately, these fault-tolerance strategies are considered essential for building resilient systems that can withstand partial failures without compromising overall service continuity, ensuring that the system remains operational even under adverse conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-091d584fced301b442654dd8c23b3fc9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3def184ad8f4755ff269862ea77393dd-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8ffe9a587b126f152ed3d89a146b445-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-202cb962ac59075b964b07152d234b70-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c56ff4ce4aaf9573aa5dff913df997a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-da4fb5c6e93e74d3df8527599fa62642-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2b44928ae11fb9384c4cf38708677c48-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-73278a4a86960eeb576a8fd4c9ec6997-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7f6ffaa6bb0b408017b62254211691b5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-698d51a19d8a121ce581499d7b701668-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2723d092b63885e0d7c260cc007e8b9d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3c65c2974270fd093ee8a9bf8ae7d0b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-65b9eea6e1cc6bb9f0cd2a47751a186f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed3d2c21991e3bef5e069713af9fa6ca-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e2ef524fbf3d9fe611d5a8e90fefdc9c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f4b9ec30ad9f68f89b29639786cb62ef-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2a38a4a9316c49e5a833517c45d31070-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-93db85ed909c13838ff95ccfa94cebd9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-43ec517d68b6edd3015b3edc9a11367b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1fe173d08e959397adf34b1d77e88d7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-14bfa6bb14875e45bba028a21ed38046-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-735b90b4568125ed6c3f678819b6e058-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-72b32a1f754ba1c09b3695e0cb6cde7f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9f61408e3afb633e50cdf1b20de6f466-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b53b3a3d6ab90ce0268229151c9bde11-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a1158154dfa42caddbd0694a4e9bdc8-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f457c545a9ded88f18ecee47145a72c0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d9d4f495e875a2e075a1a4a6e1b9770f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a1d0c6e83f027327d8461063f4ac58a6-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">208&lt;SEP&gt;125&lt;SEP&gt;124&lt;SEP&gt;123&lt;SEP&gt;121&lt;SEP&gt;120&lt;SEP&gt;115&lt;SEP&gt;113&lt;SEP&gt;112&lt;SEP&gt;111&lt;SEP&gt;109&lt;SEP&gt;108&lt;SEP&gt;105&lt;SEP&gt;98&lt;SEP&gt;97&lt;SEP&gt;94&lt;SEP&gt;88&lt;SEP&gt;86&lt;SEP&gt;81&lt;SEP&gt;79&lt;SEP&gt;69&lt;SEP&gt;67&lt;SEP&gt;57&lt;SEP&gt;56&lt;SEP&gt;55&lt;SEP&gt;52&lt;SEP&gt;49&lt;SEP&gt;46&lt;SEP&gt;42</data>
