</node>
<node id="Semantic Cache">
  <data key="d0">Semantic Cache</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Semantic cache refers to a caching mechanism that plays a critical role in modern systems, focusing on preprocessing data, maintaining state consistency, and enabling concurrency control, retry strategies, and graceful degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;A concept referring to a caching mechanism used in modern systems to optimize data processing, ensure consistency, and enhance system performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b1d10e7bafa4421218a51b1e1f1b0ba2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-31fefc0e570cb3860f2a6d4b38c6490d-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">209&lt;SEP&gt;187</data>
  <data key="d5">1788256254</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Retry Strategies">
  <data key="d0">Retry Strategies</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Retry strategies refer to methods for handling service failures by retrying operations to improve reliability.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b1d10e7bafa4421218a51b1e1f1b0ba2-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">209</data>
  <data key="d5">1788255975</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Graceful Degradation">
  <data key="d0">Graceful Degradation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Graceful degradation is a technique used to maintain essential functionality when a system or its components encounter failures.&lt;SEP&gt;Graceful Degradation is a fail-safe method used to maintain system usability in case of service anomalies in Consistent Hashing systems.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique ensuring service functionality despite dependency service failures, maintaining partial operation.&lt;SEP&gt;A strategy that ensures system availability by reducing functionality when dependent services fail.&lt;SEP&gt;A strategy to ensure system availability by offering reduced functionality during service disruptions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b1d10e7bafa4421218a51b1e1f1b0ba2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7eabe3a1649ffa2b3ff8c02ebfd5659f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-84d9ee44e457ddef7f2c4f25dc8fa865-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9dcb88e0137649590b755372b040afad-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ec5decca5ed3d6b8079e2e7e7bacc9f2-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">209&lt;SEP&gt;206&lt;SEP&gt;199&lt;SEP&gt;188&lt;SEP&gt;127</data>
  <data key="d5">1788256368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Latency Percentile">
  <data key="d0">Latency Percentile</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Latency Percentile is a core performance and monitoring metric used to measure and represent the distribution of system response times or operation latency, particularly in modern and distributed systems such as knowledge graph systems, document sharding workflows, and distributed index systems. Instead of relying on a single average value, this metric focuses on specific thresholds—most commonly the 50th (median), 95th, and 99th percentiles—to indicate the proportion of requests that meet certain speed thresholds and to highlight how often various delay values are experienced.

As a foundational tool for performance analysis, Latency Percentile captures latency distribution patterns at defined thresholds, enabling targeted analysis of system delays. By tracking these high-percentile delays, the metric helps identify potential performance bottlenecks, variations in user experience, and system delay behavior under different load conditions. It is considered one of the three core monitoring metrics requiring attention in distributed index systems, serving as an essential indicator for understanding data processing delays and guiding optimization efforts to improve overall system efficiency and responsiveness.&lt;SEP&gt;A core monitoring metric indicating latency distribution at various percentiles.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b1d10e7bafa4421218a51b1e1f1b0ba2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-274ad4786c3abca69fa097b85867d9a4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0e65972dce68dad4d52d063967f0a705-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-85d8ce590ad8981ca2c8286f79f59954-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-58a2fc6ed39fd083f55d4182bf88826d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a2557a7b2e94197ff767970b67041697-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9dcb88e0137649590b755372b040afad-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-65ded5353c5ee48d0b7d48c591b8f430-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1afa34a7f984eeabdbb0a7d494132ee5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ec5decca5ed3d6b8079e2e7e7bacc9f2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-069059b7ef840f0c74a814ec9237b6ec-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26657d5ff9020d2abefe558796b99584-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3ef815416f775098fe977004015c6193-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fe9fc289c3ff0af142b6d3bead98a923-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbd7939d674997cdb4692d34de8633c4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7f39f8317fbdb1988ef4c628eba02591-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">209&lt;SEP&gt;204&lt;SEP&gt;198&lt;SEP&gt;197&lt;SEP&gt;192&lt;SEP&gt;189&lt;SEP&gt;188&lt;SEP&gt;132&lt;SEP&gt;131&lt;SEP&gt;127&lt;SEP&gt;126&lt;SEP&gt;96&lt;SEP&gt;85&lt;SEP&gt;83&lt;SEP&gt;76&lt;SEP&gt;61</data>
  <data key="d5">1788256836</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="向量数据库">
  <data key="d0">向量数据库</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A system that plays a critical role in modern systems by managing and processing vector data, focusing on consistency, throughput, latency, and fault tolerance.&lt;SEP&gt;向量数据库是一种现代系统组件，负责存储和管理向量数据，在本文档中作为核心讨论对象，涵盖其原理、架构与工程实践。文中详细介绍了其内部机制，包括数据预处理、批次处理、状态一致性维护、并发控制、队列缓冲、重试与降级等关键技术点。&lt;SEP&gt;A modern database system designed for vector data management, handling preprocessing, batch processing, and state consistency under varying loads.&lt;SEP&gt;向量数据库是一种现代系统中承担关键角色的技术，本文档详细介绍了其核心概念、架构与工程实践，包括原理、实现、监控指标和常见问题处理。&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-69adc1e107f7f7d035d7baf04342e1ca-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3def184ad8f4755ff269862ea77393dd-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f0935e4cd5920aa6c7c996a5ee53a70f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f7177163c833dff4b38fc8d2872f1ec6-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">207&lt;SEP&gt;125&lt;SEP&gt;106&lt;SEP&gt;44</data>
  <data key="d5">1788256986</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="重试">
  <data key="d0">重试</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">重试 is a fault-handling and fallback strategy used in modern computing environments to manage transient or temporary failures in dependent services by reattempting failed operations, requests, or processing tasks. Its primary purpose is to enhance system resilience, reliability, and availability, ensuring that operations remain uninterrupted despite occasional service outages, disruptions, or anomalies in dependency components. This mechanism is particularly important in systems that rely on multiple service dependencies or streaming computation frameworks, where automatic resending or reattempting of failed requests helps mitigate the impact of instability and supports eventual operational success.

As a fault-tolerance technique, 重试 functions as a failover and recovery mechanism, directly addressing scenarios where dependent services experience abnormalities, exceptions, or errors. By systematically retrying failed operations, it maintains service continuity and adapts to dependency issues, thereby improving overall system robustness. It is explicitly recognized as a key method to guarantee availability when dependent services fail or encounter errors, and it is applied within specific contexts such as the 评估基准 system, where it serves as a critical safeguard against dependency-related disruptions. It is also used as a fallback technique in semantic caching systems to maintain availability when dependent services encounter errors.

In practice, 重试 involves the system automatically re-sending requests or reprocessing tasks to overcome temporary faults, contributing to a more stable and dependable operational environment. It is described as an essential component for maintaining service continuity in distributed or dependency-heavy architectures, and it is one of the internal mechanisms discussed in the context of 熔断降级's principles and implementation. As a recovery mechanism, it tolerates transient failures and enables continued operation, reinforcing its role as a critical safeguard for system dependability.&lt;SEP&gt;A fault-tolerance mechanism that retries failed operations when dependent services encounter exceptions.&lt;SEP&gt;A fallback mechanism used to ensure availability when dependent services encounter errors.&lt;SEP&gt;A strategy used to ensure availability when dependent services experience anomalies.&lt;SEP&gt;A fallback strategy used to maintain availability when dependency services encounter exceptions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-69adc1e107f7f7d035d7baf04342e1ca-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3644a684f98ea8fe223c713b77189a77-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-757b505cfd34c64c85ca5b5690ee5293-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-854d6fae5ee42911677c739ee1734486-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-084b6fbb10729ed4da8c3d3f5a3ae7c9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a597e50502f5ff68e3e25b9114205d4a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9fc3d7152ba9336a670e36d0ed79bc43-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1f491a404d6854880943e5c3cd9ca25-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb160de1de89d9058fcb0b968dbbbd68-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5fd0b37cd7dbbb00f97ba6ce92bf5add-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5f93f983524def3dca464469d2cf9f3e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a97da629b098b75c294dffdc3e463904-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c9e1074f5b3f9fc8ea15d152add07294-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ec8956637a99787bd197eacd77acce5e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-38b3eff8baf56627478ec76a704e9b52-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f899139df5e1059396431415e770c6dd-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ac627ab1ccbdb62ec96e702f07f6425b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98dce83da57b0395e163467c9dae521b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54229abfcfa5649e7003b83dd4755294-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c7e1249ffc03eb9ded908c236bd1996d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-68d30a9594728bc39aa24be94b319d21-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f033ab37c30201f73f142449d037028d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ad61ab143223efbc24c7d2583be69251-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d2ddea18f00665ce8623e36bd4e3c7c5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-32bb90e8976aab5298d5da10fe66f21d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7cbbc409ec990f19c78c75bd1e06f215-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3f390d88e4c41f2747bfa2f1b5f87db-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3295c76acbf4caaed33c36b1b5fc2cb1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fc490ca45c00b1249bbe3554a4fdf6fb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-03afdbd66e7929b125f8597834fa83a4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66f041e16a60928b05a7e228a89c3799-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a684eceee76fc522773286a895bc8436-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d82c8d1619ad8176d665453cfb2e55f0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2838023a778dfaecdc212708f721b788-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c0c7c76d30bd3dcaefc96f40275bdc0a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-67c6a1e7ce56d3d6fa748ab6d9af3fd7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-17e62166fc8586dfa4d1bc0e1742c08b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3416a75f4cea9109507cacd8e2f2aefc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d645920e395fedad7bbbed0eca3fe2e0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5771bce93e200c36f7cd9dfd0e5deaa-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">207&lt;SEP&gt;200&lt;SEP&gt;201&lt;SEP&gt;202&lt;SEP&gt;196&lt;SEP&gt;194&lt;SEP&gt;133&lt;SEP&gt;129&lt;SEP&gt;117&lt;SEP&gt;114&lt;SEP&gt;110&lt;SEP&gt;107&lt;SEP&gt;104&lt;SEP&gt;102&lt;SEP&gt;101&lt;SEP&gt;100&lt;SEP&gt;99&lt;SEP&gt;93&lt;SEP&gt;91&lt;SEP&gt;87&lt;SEP&gt;84&lt;SEP&gt;80&lt;SEP&gt;74&lt;SEP&gt;73&lt;SEP&gt;72&lt;SEP&gt;70&lt;SEP&gt;68&lt;SEP&gt;66&lt;SEP&gt;65&lt;SEP&gt;63&lt;SEP&gt;58&lt;SEP&gt;54&lt;SEP&gt;53&lt;SEP&gt;51&lt;SEP&gt;50&lt;SEP&gt;47&lt;SEP&gt;43&lt;SEP&gt;41&lt;SEP&gt;40&lt;SEP&gt;38</data>
  <data key="d5">1788257034</data>
