</node>
<node id="Consistent Hashing">
  <data key="d0">Consistent Hashing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Consistent Hashing is a core concept widely used in modern systems for distributing data, ensuring state consistency, and managing traffic and failures.&lt;SEP&gt;A hashing technique that plays a key role in modern systems, ensuring consistent state maintenance and load distribution across batches.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7eabe3a1649ffa2b3ff8c02ebfd5659f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fe9fc289c3ff0af142b6d3bead98a923-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">206&lt;SEP&gt;83</data>
  <data key="d5">1788256668</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Network Round-Trip Latency">
  <data key="d0">Network Round-Trip Latency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Network Round-Trip Latency measures the time delay for data to travel between remote services in Consistent Hashing systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The time taken for a request to reach a remote service and for the response to return.&lt;SEP&gt;A performance metric referring to the time taken for data to travel to and from remote services, which can be excessively high and impact system performance.&lt;SEP&gt;A common issue involving excessive latency in remote service network calls.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7eabe3a1649ffa2b3ff8c02ebfd5659f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0e65972dce68dad4d52d063967f0a705-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-069059b7ef840f0c74a814ec9237b6ec-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-093f65e080a295f8076b1c5722a46aa2-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">206&lt;SEP&gt;198&lt;SEP&gt;126&lt;SEP&gt;59</data>
  <data key="d5">1788256850</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Attribution Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Attribution Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Attribution Analysis is a technique used to identify root causes of performance issues, such as slow queries, in Consistent Hashing systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7eabe3a1649ffa2b3ff8c02ebfd5659f-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">206</data>
  <data key="d5">1788256010</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Evidence Chain">
  <data key="d0">Evidence Chain</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An Evidence Chain is a structured and methodical record used to document and validate changes within a system, particularly in the context of distributed systems, Consistent Hashing, and semantic caching. It functions by retaining comparative data—typically metrics and results—collected both before and after parameter adjustments or tuning decisions are implemented. This before-and-after documentation serves as the foundational evidence for verifying that a specific change had the intended impact, enabling analysts to confirm the validity of system modifications and tuning choices.

The Evidence Chain is designed to support verification and analysis by preserving a clear, traceable history of system performance. It acts as a system of documentation that provides a comprehensive view of the effects of alterations, ensuring that every significant change is backed by measurable proof. By systematically capturing this comparative data, the Evidence Chain facilitates evidence-based decision-making and helps validate that adjustments to system parameters, such as those affecting Document Slicing Strategies, produce the desired outcomes without unintended regressions.&lt;SEP&gt;Documentation of before-and-after comparisons required for any parameter tuning changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Documentation of before-and-after comparisons for any parameter changes.&lt;SEP&gt;A record of before-and-after comparison data used to validate the effect of system changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7eabe3a1649ffa2b3ff8c02ebfd5659f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0e65972dce68dad4d52d063967f0a705-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-85d8ce590ad8981ca2c8286f79f59954-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-bd686fd640be98efaae0091fa301e613-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cfecdb276f634854f3ef915e2e980c31-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-31fefc0e570cb3860f2a6d4b38c6490d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9b8619251a19057cff70779273e95aa6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-812b4ba287f5ee0bc9d43bbf5bbe87fb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3ef815416f775098fe977004015c6193-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7f39f8317fbdb1988ef4c628eba02591-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-072b030ba126b2f4b2374f342be9ed44-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">206&lt;SEP&gt;198&lt;SEP&gt;197&lt;SEP&gt;193&lt;SEP&gt;190&lt;SEP&gt;187&lt;SEP&gt;130&lt;SEP&gt;95&lt;SEP&gt;85&lt;SEP&gt;61&lt;SEP&gt;60</data>
  <data key="d5">1788256843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="嵌入模型">
  <data key="d0">嵌入模型</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">嵌入模型（Embedding Model）是一个在现代系统中承担关键角色的核心概念与系统组件，其核心职责是将数据转换为向量表示，以支持各类机器学习任务，并在此基础上承担数据处理与状态维护的重要职能。该模型在运行机制上遵循一套系统化的架构与方法论，通常先对数据进行预处理，随后按批次（batch）进行处理，并在整个过程中严格维护系统状态的一致性。为了保障系统在高负载或依赖服务出现异常时依然具备高可用性与数据一致性，嵌入模型引入了多项工程机制，包括并发控制、队列缓冲、重试机制以及降级（fallback）方案。此外，该系统还注重对性能指标的监控与调优，重点关注吞吐量、延迟百分位数以及错误率等关键数据，以支撑系统稳定运行与持续优化。该实体在本文档中被作为技术详解的主题，围绕其原理、架构设计及工程实践进行了系统阐述，旨在说明嵌入模型如何通过预处理、批处理、一致性保障及容错机制，在现代系统中高效、可靠地完成数据处理任务。</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eae27d77ca20db309e056e3d2dcd7d69-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a597e50502f5ff68e3e25b9114205d4a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-76dc611d6ebaafc66cc0879c71b5db5c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2723d092b63885e0d7c260cc007e8b9d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2a38a4a9316c49e5a833517c45d31070-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-14bfa6bb14875e45bba028a21ed38046-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f457c545a9ded88f18ecee47145a72c0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6c8349cc7260ae62e3b1396831a8398f-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">205&lt;SEP&gt;194&lt;SEP&gt;128&lt;SEP&gt;109&lt;SEP&gt;88&lt;SEP&gt;69&lt;SEP&gt;49&lt;SEP&gt;45</data>
  <data key="d5">1788256980</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="复验生成文档">
  <data key="d0">复验生成文档</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A document created for re-verification processes, specifically used in Stage 4 for regression analysis within data import pipelines.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eae27d77ca20db309e056e3d2dcd7d69-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">205</data>
  <data key="d5">1788256018</data>
