</node>
<node id="重试机制">
  <data key="d0">重试机制</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">重试机制（Retry Mechanism）is a fault tolerance and reliability technique used in distributed systems and software architecture to ensure system availability when dependent services encounter exceptions, errors, or failures. As a fallback strategy, it operates by reattempting failed operations—such as network requests, database calls, or external API invocations—with the goal of maintaining overall system reliability and continuity of service. The mechanism is specifically designed to handle transient faults or temporary unavailability in downstream components, thereby preventing a single failure from cascading into broader system outages. By automatically retrying failed operations, the retry mechanism enhances the robustness and resilience of dependent systems, allowing them to recover from short-lived disruptions without requiring manual intervention. This approach is widely applied in scenarios where high availability is critical, and it serves as a practical means to improve the success rate of operations and uphold service-level agreements in complex, interconnected environments.&lt;SEP&gt;依赖服务异常时保证可用性的策略。&lt;SEP&gt;当依赖服务出现异常时，嵌入模型用于保证可用性的手段之一。&lt;SEP&gt;当依赖服务异常时采用的策略，通过重试来保证系统的可用性。&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;A failure-handling strategy that retries operations when dependent services behave abnormally.&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eae27d77ca20db309e056e3d2dcd7d69-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7f1de29e6da19d22b51c68001e7e0e54-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6974ce5ac660610b44d9b9fed0ff9548-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8613985ec49eb8f757ae6439e879bb2a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9778d5d219c5080b9a6a17bef029331c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35f4a8d465e6e1edc05f3d8ab658c551-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d09bf41544a3365a46c9077ebb5e35c3-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e2c420d928d4bf8ce0ff2ec19b371514-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-642e92efb79421734881b53e1e1b18b6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6c8349cc7260ae62e3b1396831a8398f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f7177163c833dff4b38fc8d2872f1ec6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d67d8ab4f4c10bf22aa353e27879133c-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">205&lt;SEP&gt;135&lt;SEP&gt;103&lt;SEP&gt;90&lt;SEP&gt;82&lt;SEP&gt;78&lt;SEP&gt;75&lt;SEP&gt;71&lt;SEP&gt;48&lt;SEP&gt;45&lt;SEP&gt;44&lt;SEP&gt;39</data>
  <data key="d5">1788257032</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="降级机制">
  <data key="d0">降级机制</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">降级机制（Degradation Mechanism）是一种在依赖服务发生异常或系统发生故障时，通过临时缩减功能范围、简化处理流程或降低服务能力，以保障核心业务连续性和系统整体可用性的系统性技术手段与策略。该机制通常与重试（retry）机制结合使用，共同构成保证系统在部分组件失效情况下依然能够对外提供基本服务能力的韧性设计。

降级机制的核心目标并非恢复全部功能，而是在无法提供完整服务的前提下，主动、有意识地选择放弃非核心功能或非关键数据，从而将有限的系统资源集中于维护核心操作和关键流程的正常运转。这种策略确保了当依赖服务出现异常时，系统不会因为个别组件的故障而完全瘫痪，而是通过功能降级的方式实现部分服务可用性，最大程度降低对用户体验和业务连续性的负面影响。在实际工程实践中，降级机制被视为保障微服务架构和分布式系统高可用性的关键手段之一，其设计与实施需充分考虑业务优先级、降级触发条件及恢复策略，以确保系统在稳定状态下沉降级操作能够平滑恢复。</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eae27d77ca20db309e056e3d2dcd7d69-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7f1de29e6da19d22b51c68001e7e0e54-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6974ce5ac660610b44d9b9fed0ff9548-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8613985ec49eb8f757ae6439e879bb2a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35f4a8d465e6e1edc05f3d8ab658c551-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e2c420d928d4bf8ce0ff2ec19b371514-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6c8349cc7260ae62e3b1396831a8398f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f7177163c833dff4b38fc8d2872f1ec6-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">205&lt;SEP&gt;135&lt;SEP&gt;103&lt;SEP&gt;90&lt;SEP&gt;78&lt;SEP&gt;71&lt;SEP&gt;45&lt;SEP&gt;44</data>
  <data key="d5">1788256990</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Document Slicing Strategy">
  <data key="d0">Document Slicing Strategy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A strategy for slicing documents, including its core concepts, architecture, and engineering practices, used in modern system processes.&lt;SEP&gt;A core concept in modern systems involving the segmentation of documents into smaller, manageable parts for processing and analysis. It emphasizes maintaining state consistency, controlling concurrency, buffering queues, and handling exceptions to ensure availability and performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-274ad4786c3abca69fa097b85867d9a4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-85d8ce590ad8981ca2c8286f79f59954-chunk-000</data>
