  <data key="d2">A data masking technology that is the central subject of the technical document, covering core concepts, architecture, and engineering practices.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;A technical practice that anonymizes or masks sensitive data in modern systems, discussed across sections for its core concepts, architecture, and engineering implementation, including preprocessing, batching, state consistency, concurrency control, queue buffering, retries, degradation, monitoring metrics, and performance tuning.&lt;SEP&gt;A data masking technology and its detailed principles, architecture, and engineering practices discussed in the document. It is described as playing a key role in modern systems, involving preprocessing, main flow processing, batch handling, state consistency, concurrency control, queue buffering, retry, degradation, and monitoring of throughput, latency percentiles, and error rates.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;A technique for masking sensitive data in modern systems, involving preprocessing, batch processing, and state consistency maintenance. Also the subject of the test document.</data>
