<edge source="吞吐量" target="监控">
  <data key="d7">17.0</data>
  <data key="d8">(吞吐量, 监控) is a relation that defines the monitoring of throughput as a fundamental and integral aspect of system performance evaluation, particularly within streaming computation systems. Throughput, as a metric, is continuously tracked to assess how efficiently a system processes data, serving as a critical indicator of overall operational health and capacity. The monitoring activity is deliberate and analytical, designed to detect processing speed variations, identify potential bottlenecks, and support real-time oversight and long-term performance tuning.

The relation consistently emphasizes that throughput is treated as a core indicator alongside other metrics, not as a peripheral measure. In practice, monitoring focuses on throughput to gauge data processing efficiency, with the activity being central to the system's evaluation framework. This ensures that system capacity and responsiveness are consistently measured, allowing for adjustments based on measurable data. The descriptions uniformly highlight that throughput monitoring aims to maintain and optimize system operations, ensuring computational systems meet performance expectations and operate efficiently. Overall, (吞吐量, 监控) encapsulates the practice of prioritizing throughput in monitoring efforts as one of the primary benchmarks, supporting both immediate operational health checks and sustained performance enhancement.&lt;SEP&gt;Monitoring tracks the throughput metric to assess system performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Monitoring tracks throughput as a core metric.</data>
