<edge source="延迟分位数" target="监控">
  <data key="d7">17.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Latency percentiles (延迟分位数) are a core metric monitored by monitoring (监控) systems to evaluate system latency performance. The monitoring process tracks these percentiles to assess the distribution of processing times and response time distributions, particularly in streaming computation environments. As a key performance indicator, latency percentiles provide a comprehensive view of system responsiveness and processing efficiency by focusing on delays. Monitoring frameworks explicitly include latency percentiles as one of their core metrics, often highlighted alongside other primary indicators. The monitoring activity is specifically designed to track latency percentiles to gain insights into delay distributions, making it an essential component for performance assessment. In practice, monitoring systems use latency percentiles to measure and record processing time variations, ensuring that system behavior aligns with performance expectations. Latency percentiles serve as a fundamental and consistently emphasized metric within monitoring frameworks, integral to evaluating and optimizing system latency and overall operational health.&lt;SEP&gt;Monitoring tracks latency percentiles to understand response time distribution.&lt;SEP&gt;Monitoring tracks latency percentiles as a core metric.</data>
  <data key="d9">connected to,evaluation,measure,measures,monitored by,monitoring,monitors,tracks,关注,关注指标,指标监控,指标监测,跟踪</data>
