<edge source="错误率" target="监控">
  <data key="d7">17.0</data>
  <data key="d8">(监控, 错误率) is a relation that defines the monitoring and tracking of the error rate as a core metric within a system, particularly in the context of streaming computation. This relation establishes error rate as a key performance indicator (KPI) used to evaluate system stability and operational health. Through this relation, the monitoring process observes, analyzes, and evaluates the frequency of failures or errors occurring in the system, thereby providing insight into the overall reliability and performance of the streaming computation environment.

The relation emphasizes that error rate is not merely a passive statistic but an actively tracked and assessed measurement, integrated into the broader monitoring framework. It functions as one of the primary indicators for performance assessment, meaning that fluctuations in the error rate are closely watched to detect anomalies, diagnose issues, and trigger corrective actions. By systematically tracking the error rate, the monitoring system helps ensure that the system remains stable and that any increase in errors is promptly addressed to maintain service quality.

Overall, (监控, 错误率) represents a fundamental component of system oversight, where the error rate serves as a critical signal for both real-time monitoring and long-term performance evaluation in distributed or streaming data processing systems. Notably, error rate is consistently identified as one of the three core indicators within this monitoring framework, along with other essential metrics, and its tracking is central to identifying the proportion of failures and facilitating timely interventions.&lt;SEP&gt;Monitoring tracks the error rate to assess system health.&lt;SEP&gt;Monitoring tracks error rate as a core metric.</data>
  <data key="d9">connected to,evaluation,measure,measures,monitored by,monitoring,monitors,tracks,关注,关注指标,指标监控,指标监测,跟踪</data>
