<edge source="压测" target="缓存失效风暴">
  <data key="d7">42.0</data>
  <data key="d8">压测 (stress testing) is a pre-deployment methodology specifically employed to detect and address cache failure storms, also known as cache stampedes or cache invalidation storms. This proactive approach simulates high-load conditions to expose and manage vulnerabilities that arise when a cache expires or is invalidated, causing multiple concurrent requests to regenerate cached data and resulting in a surge of backend load. The primary goal is to identify and mitigate such critical issues before a system goes live, thereby ensuring system stability, resilience, and preventing potential downtime or service degradation in a production environment.

Load testing is utilized both to expose the existence of cache invalidation storm problems and to verify that mitigation strategies are effective. This pre-release testing phase is critical because cache stampedes are a frequent and well-known performance risk; if left unaddressed, they can overwhelm backend resources and cause cascading failures. By deliberately inducing these conditions in a controlled test environment, engineers can observe system behavior under stress, evaluate the effectiveness of safeguards such as request coalescing or early recomputation, and implement necessary fixes.

In practice, 压测 helps expose issues such as cache invalidation storms before system deployment, making it a common and essential step in system evaluation. By integrating this practice into the deployment workflow, teams resolve these issues prior to launch, reinforcing the importance of proactive testing for a robust and reliable system. Ultimately, incorporating 压测 into the deployment workflow ensures that cache-related vulnerabilities are identified and resolved prior to launch, contributing to a more resilient and dependable production system.&lt;SEP&gt;Load testing exposes cache invalidation storms before deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;缓存失效风暴为实践中常见问题，需通过压测在上线前暴露。&lt;SEP&gt;Performance testing (压测) is conducted before deployment to expose issues such as cache invalidation storms.&lt;SEP&gt;压测在上线前暴露缓存失效风暴等问题。&lt;SEP&gt;Cache invalidation storms are exposed through load testing.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Stress testing exposes cache invalidation storms before deployment.</data>
