<edge source="压测" target="远程服务网络往返延迟">
  <data key="d7">21.0</data>
  <data key="d8">压测 (Stress Testing), also referred to as load testing in some contexts, is a performance testing methodology employed to expose and manage high remote service network round-trip latency issues before a system is deployed to production or released. The primary objective of this approach is to identify and quantify latency problems associated with communication with remote services, thereby verifying the system’s tolerance to network delays and guiding the optimization of its communication pathways. By simulating adverse network conditions, stress testing enables development teams to observe and measure network delays, ensuring that potential performance bottlenecks are detected and addressed prior to a live release.

This practice serves as a critical pre-deployment checkpoint, confirming that latency-related risks are understood, mitigated, and that the system can maintain stability and responsiveness under unfavorable conditions. The ultimate goal is to validate that the system is prepared for real-world operational demands, with high remote service network round-trip latency being proactively addressed through systematic testing.&lt;SEP&gt;压测is used to expose high远程服务网络往返延迟as a potential issue before going live.&lt;SEP&gt;压测is used to expose high远程服务网络往返延迟before deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;High network round-trip delays with remote services are expected to be exposed by load testing before deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;High remote service network round-trip latency is exposed through load testing.&lt;SEP&gt;Load testing exposes high remote service network round-trip latency before deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;Performance testing is used to expose high remote service network latency issues before deployment.</data>
