<edge source="压测" target="参数调优">
  <data key="d7">13.0</data>
  <data key="d8">(压测, 参数调优) is a data-driven relationship in which parameter tuning is fundamentally dependent on the empirical evidence obtained through stress testing (压测). This relationship emphasizes that all decisions regarding parameter adjustments must be grounded in measured data collected from load testing rather than relying on intuition or unverified assumptions. The stress testing process serves as the primary source of quantitative information, supplying the necessary benchmarks and performance metrics that inform the tuning process.

Parameter tuning, as guided by this relationship, is a systematic process that uses the results from load testing to identify optimal configuration settings. The tuning activity is not conducted in isolation but is an iterative practice where adjustments are validated by comparing performance before and after changes. This before-and-after comparison evidence is crucial, as it allows practitioners to confirm that modifications lead to tangible improvements or achieve the desired system behavior.

Moreover, the relationship underscores that the data gathered through stress testing—and potentially other measured sources—is the sole legitimate basis for making tuning decisions. This ensures that the tuning process remains objective, reproducible, and aligned with the actual operational characteristics of the system under test. Consequently, (压测, 参数调优) represents a methodological principle where load testing not only supports parameter tuning by providing actionable data but also defines the standard for how tuning should be executed: rigorously, empirically, and with clear evidence of impact.&lt;SEP&gt;参数调优应基于压测得到的实测数据，而非直觉。&lt;SEP&gt;参数调优relies on压测data for informed adjustments.&lt;SEP&gt;Parameter tuning is based on load testing data rather than intuition.&lt;SEP&gt;参数调优所依据的实测数据来源于压测等测试手段。&lt;SEP&gt;Parameter tuning should be based on measured data obtained via stress testing.</data>
  <data key="d9">based on,based_on,informed by,practice,relies_on,supports,uses,使用,依据,关联,基于,基于数据,数据,数据来源,方法,证据链</data>
