<edge source="参数调优" target="实测数据">
  <data key="d7">17.0</data>
  <data key="d8">(参数调优, 实测数据) is a relation that establishes a strict, evidence-based framework for parameter tuning in system optimization, particularly within the context of a semantic caching system. The core principle is that all parameter tuning must be grounded in measured data—referred to as 实测数据 or actual test data—rather than intuition or guesswork. This data-driven approach ensures that tuning decisions are objective, reliable, and justified by real performance metrics.

The relation mandates that parameter tuning is not a one-time adjustment but a systematic procedure requiring the preservation of an evidence chain. This evidence chain must document the before-and-after states of any change, enabling transparent comparisons and validating the effectiveness of each modification. The requirement applies universally across all aspects of the system, ensuring every parameter change is backed by actual performance data and that the entire process supports informed decision-making.

In summary, (参数调优, 实测数据) defines parameter tuning as a rigorous, measurement-driven discipline where measured data dictates the direction of optimization, and comprehensive records of changes are maintained for thorough evaluation. This ensures that all adjustments are verifiable and contribute to reliable system performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Parameter tuning in multi-channel recall is based on measured data rather than intuition.&lt;SEP&gt;参数调优应基于实测数据而非直觉。</data>
