<edge source="主流程" target="预处理">
  <data key="d7">20.0</data>
  <data key="d8">(主流程, 预处理) is a unidirectional, foundational relation within data processing systems, defining that preprocessing acts as a mandatory precursor to the main workflow. This relation establishes a strict temporal and functional sequence: preprocessing operates on raw or incoming data—cleansing, formatting, or otherwise preparing it—before that data is introduced into the primary flow. The main workflow, which can be a streaming computation system, a data masking system, an evaluation benchmark, a query rewriting flow, a batch processing pipeline, an inverted index (倒排索引) builder, a re-ranking (重排序) system, or a tokenization algorithm, depends entirely on this upstream stage to function properly. In all contexts, preprocessing must complete its actions before the main flow begins its substantive operations, indicating that the relation is not parallel or optional but a strict feeder or preparatory step.  

The dependency is clear and consistent: preprocessing supplies processed data directly to the main flow, and the main flow consumes this prepared data as its input. There is no evidence of any reverse dependency or alternative ordering—the relation is unidirectional and foundational to the overall system architecture, regardless of the system type. For instance, data after preprocessing enters the main workflow of an inverted index, or preprocessed data is passed into the main flow of a tokenization algorithm. This core semantics remain unchanged across all cited examples, reinforcing that preprocessing prepares data, and the main flow consumes it, with no parallel or optional role for the preprocessing stage. The relation thus defines a critical handoff point in the data pipeline, ensuring the main workflow receives only data that has been properly prepared.&lt;SEP&gt;Preprocessed data is fed into the main processing flow.&lt;SEP&gt;Data enters the main flow after undergoing preprocessing.&lt;SEP&gt;Preprocessed data enters the main workflow in multi-channel recall.&lt;SEP&gt;Preprocessed data enters the main flow of the document slicing strategy.&lt;SEP&gt;Data passes through preprocessing before entering the main flow.</data>
  <data key="d9">data flow,depends_on,feeds,feeds into,feeds_into,flow,inputs,precedes,sequencing,前置,流程,流程顺序,输入,进入</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-3644a684f98ea8fe223c713b77189a77-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c56ff4ce4aaf9573aa5dff913df997a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eb160de1de89d9058fcb0b968dbbbd68-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5fd0b37cd7dbbb00f97ba6ce92bf5add-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-73278a4a86960eeb576a8fd4c9ec6997-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3c65c2974270fd093ee8a9bf8ae7d0b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6974ce5ac660610b44d9b9fed0ff9548-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f899139df5e1059396431415e770c6dd-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ac627ab1ccbdb62ec96e702f07f6425b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e2ef524fbf3d9fe611d5a8e90fefdc9c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c7e1249ffc03eb9ded908c236bd1996d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-68d30a9594728bc39aa24be94b319d21-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7cbbc409ec990f19c78c75bd1e06f215-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9f61408e3afb633e50cdf1b20de6f466-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a684eceee76fc522773286a895bc8436-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d82c8d1619ad8176d665453cfb2e55f0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c0c7c76d30bd3dcaefc96f40275bdc0a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a1158154dfa42caddbd0694a4e9bdc8-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-17e62166fc8586dfa4d1bc0e1742c08b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a5771bce93e200c36f7cd9dfd0e5deaa-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d11">200&lt;SEP&gt;121&lt;SEP&gt;117&lt;SEP&gt;114&lt;SEP&gt;113&lt;SEP&gt;108&lt;SEP&gt;103&lt;SEP&gt;100&lt;SEP&gt;99&lt;SEP&gt;97&lt;SEP&gt;87&lt;SEP&gt;84&lt;SEP&gt;70&lt;SEP&gt;56&lt;SEP&gt;54&lt;SEP&gt;53&lt;SEP&gt;50&lt;SEP&gt;52&lt;SEP&gt;43&lt;SEP&gt;38</data>
